<DocsLayout title="Deployment models" description="Use an explicit contract: Dockerfile, Docker Compose, static/SPA, or a public OCI image.">
<section><p class="overline">Current modes</p><h2>Four deployment paths</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Mode</th><th>Execution</th><th>Recovery</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Git</td><td><code>dockerfile</code></td><td>Build the repository Dockerfile and run the resulting image.</td><td>Historical rollback</td></tr><tr><td>Git</td><td><code>compose</code></td><td>Resolve Compose configuration, start the services, and route the selected public service.</td><td>Historical rollback</td></tr><tr><td>Git</td><td><code>static</code></td><td>Build when required, publish an atomic static release, and serve it through Caddy.</td><td>Redeploy / roll-forward</td></tr><tr><td>Registry</td><td><code>image</code></td><td>Pull a public OCI image and run it through the managed runtime lifecycle.</td><td>Historical rollback</td></tr></tbody></table><aside class="note"><p>Registry deployment currently targets public images. Private registry credential management is outside the current implementation.</p></aside></section>
<section><h2>Git source detection</h2><ol class="steps"><li>Discover and rank Compose candidates.</li><li>Otherwise use a production Dockerfile when available.</li><li>Otherwise detect a static site or static SPA.</li><li>Use Nixpacks only as an additional framework/provider inspection signal.</li></ol><p>Nixpacks is not a deployment mode. Backend or SSR projects without Compose or a production Dockerfile are asked to provide an explicit production contract.</p></section>
<section><h2>Dockerfile</h2><p>MyPaaS builds the configured Dockerfile, starts the managed runtime with the selected resources, and activates the Caddy route after the replacement runtime is ready.</p></section>
<section><h2>Docker Compose</h2><p>Compose projects can use files below the repository root, ordered override files, profiles, explicit working directories, a selected public service, and per-service resource overrides. Logs and metrics remain available with service context.</p></section>
<section><h2>Static / SPA</h2><p>Static projects have no persistent application container. When a supported project needs a build, MyPaaS can run a bounded build, publish the resulting release atomically, and serve it directly through Caddy. SPA history routes fall back to the release <code>index.html</code>.</p></section>
<section><h2>Public OCI image</h2><p>Registry projects can deploy compatible public images from sources such as Docker Hub or GHCR. They use the normal lifecycle, resource, routing, log, metric, and rollback model but do not use Git webhooks.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
